coreinfo - inspect a process core dump

SYNOPSIS
    coreinfo file ...

DESCRIPTION
    For each file, display the process ID, owner ID, signal, memory
    size, and saved general-purpose registers. The size reported is
    the memory payload measured in the file.

    Project9 writes a private core.PID in the process's working
    directory when it can dump a process that quits with SIGQUIT.
    One filesystem file bounds how much of the address space can
    be saved. A dump may contain private data from the process.

EXIT STATUS
    0   Each file contains the advertised core data.
    1   A file is unreadable, invalid, or incomplete.
    2   No file was supplied.

SEE ALSO
    kill(1), console(5)
